1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Henricus Andersson Laurila was born 13 November 1781 in Nakkila. The church confirmation records say scholaris, in other words a student or a pupil. His last name was Agnell back then, because a student had to have a last name. He
2 CONC  studied in the Turku trivial school (a four year school before high school) and then in the Turku Academy for several years but didn't really complete any degree.  He was a volunteer in the military (drafted) between 16 August an
2 CONC d 16 October 1808. His plan was probably to stay in the service but the profession wasn't suitable for him after all. He wasn't really an officer, but after going back to civilian world, he used the title of vänrikki (2nd lieutena
2 CONC nt). In the Nakkila confirmation records, there is also a blurred word "tenviolist" so was he also a musician?  Between 1812 and 1818 he lived in Lammainen village of Nakkila with his mother and the maid Anna Lisa Pehrsdotter.  Re
2 CONC cords show them having moved to Kumo 6 February 1820; Harjavalta was back then a chapel parish of Kokemäki and they actually moved to Harjavalta, where they settled in Alanen in Näähälä.  He died in 1821 in Harjavalta.
2 CONT
2 CONT Muuttokirja Harjavaltaan 2.2.1820. On naimaton. Käyttää patronyymiä Andersson sukunimenään Harjavalta muuttokirjoja 1819-1833 (AP I Jba:2)  Nackila: Fändricken Herr Hendrich Andersson ; SSHY http://www.sukuhistoria.fi/sshy/sivut/j
2 CONC asenille/paikat.php?bid=13815&pnum=73 / Viitattu 11.05.2021
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrikin kuoltua vaimo avioituu heti uudelleen. Muuttokirjan mukaan tytär Henrika on syntynyt avioliiton ulkopuolella mutta poika Henrik on 1 avioliitosta. Vaimon muuttokirja Kokemäelle v 1823. Muuttokirja http://digi.narc.fi/digi
2 CONC /view.ka?kuid=7246752
