2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Owned the Hammas horse farm in Havinki.  He was born February 2, 1822 in Harjavalta. Born in the Alanen farm of Harjavalta, but Henrik's father was already dead then. Henrik Tertullian's mother remarried soon, her second husband w
2 CONC as smith Johan Stenfors and the family moved to a Kokemäki village of Ylistaro, to a sharecropper's farm called Piitari (or to a part of it).  Henrik Tertullian moved from the Kokemäki village of Ylistaro to Harjavalta, to the Ham
2 CONC mas farm in the village of Havinki, after having bought the farm on August 24, 1845 and the same year he married Mari Elisa Tupi. The Hammas farm Henrik Tertullian bought from his Cousin Marjaana Kristiina Laurila's husband Lars H
2 CONC enrik Lauren. Eero Haviala (Jul 2001) "Henrik had himself built later a house further from the river, where he lived for the rest of his life. This house is still standing. Eero Haviala would have bought it, but it had already bee
2 CONC n sold to somebody outside the family. The Hammas house, where Henrik lived earlier, has been torn down."  He died on June 18, 1891 in Harjavalta.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henric Tertulianus Andersson 2.2.1822. Äkta son af Fendric Andersson'''. Isä on kuollut ja äiti avioitunut uudelleen. Muuttokirja Harjavallan Näyhälästä Kokemäelle v 1823. Muuttokirja http://digi.narc.fi/digi/view.ka?kuid=72467
2 CONC 52
