1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Moved from Harjavalta to Pori in 1872,  and was then a bachelor.  Moved from Pori to Harjavalta on December 1, 1892 and was then in his second marriage.  His family moved with him.  He was the blacksmith on the Krekula farm in the
2 CONC  village of Vareksela in the Harjavalta parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Harjavalta parish burned down on November 11, 1889 and with it the archives too.  The fire destroyed the communion books, born children books, dead people books, marriage books, moved in and out books and all other documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justinus was born at the Hammas farm in Harjavalta on April 11 1853.  He moved from Harjavalta to Pori in 1872 to become an apprentice to a smith and later worked as a smith in Pori. The Haviala's reported about Justinus's life in
2 CONC  Pori Jul 2001: "Justinus got married in Pori to Amanda Pihala. Amanda's brother owned a smithy in Pori and (almost) a whole block in the Pori section number 6. Because Amanda's brother and his wife didn't have any children, they 
2 CONC left the business and other possessions in their will to Amanda and her husband Justinus. Justinus was a very appreciated craftsman and a popular company in Pori. The 'cream' of Pori used to party at his house and generally gather
2 CONC  there, because alcohol was always served there. Justinus, in other words, abused alcohol even before Amanda died, but after that he went downhill and started really consuming alcohol. Soon his property in Pori was almost gone."  
2 CONC His wife Amanda died in 1888 and he remarried 26 February 1890.  He and his new wife  moved to Harjavalta 1 Dec 1892. He built himself a house in Vareksela in Krekula, where he set up a smithy and therefore did some smith work. Th
2 CONC e house is still standing and living there is Justinus's son Juho's daughter Tyyne. The smithy is no longer there. The Haviala's Jul 2001: "Soon after coming to Harjavalta he lost the rest of his property in Pori one night when he
2 CONC  was playing cards in the Hälli tavern in Harjavalta. It was a real shock and he almost lost his mind, but then recovered. Justinus was a big, handsome man."  He died on March 5, 1915 in Harjavalta.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hauta Harjavallan HautausmaallaSeppä Justiinus Tertuljaanus Henrikson * 12/4 1853 † 5/3 1915 (kivi).: 
