2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT He died at the age of: 85y 1m 10d. He was a sexman at Mattila, Harjakangas. Kustaa became that farm owner at Mattila farm in Harjakangas.  In the late 1830’s  Kustaa became the seksmaanni (sexman in Swedish) for Harjakangas.  Each
2 CONC  village usually had one man who was a member of the Parish Council who saw that no one in his village was breaking the law. When anyone in the village needed an official, Kustaa was likely the one whom people first contacted.  He
2 CONC  was himself, a man of good character and known in his community as being a fair and reliable man. About 1840 Kustaa Mattila was elected as Parish Warded, being a higher official of the parish. He retained his position of seksmann
2 CONC i as well. He held both positions until the late 1850’s.  Although Mattila ws not a large farm, it was prosperous enough to support at least two farmhands and two servant girls at a time.  Contracts were usually negotiated in the 
2 CONC autumn for the following year.  The hired people at Mattila usually stayed there for two or three years before moving away. Kustaa and his two wives were usually in church for Holy Communion only once each year,  They were each re
2 CONC corded in the annual kinkeri (parish examination) as having a good understanding of their faith.  However, it was noted that Kustaa was surprising weak at reading and writing.  When it came to verbally explaining his faith, he did
2 CONC  much better. The end of 1860, Kustaa and his second wife, Marja Sofia, were living at the Mattila farm. Kustaa Mattila and his family lived at Mattila farm in Harjakangas (Ridgewoods) village, located in Noormarkku Luthern Parish
2 CONC , Pori, Finland. He was born in Eura Parish and had moved from there to Noormarkkua  couple years before he married his first wife, Eeva Kristiina Mikkola. Kustaa Mattila and his family lived at the Mattila farm in Harjakangas (Ri
2 CONC dgewoods) village, located in Noormarkku Luthern Parish, Pori Filand.He was born in Eura Parish and had moved from there to Noormarkku couple years before he married his first wife, Eeva Kristiina Mikkola. Kustaa became that farm 
2 CONC owner at Mattila farm. In the late 1830’s Kustaa became the seksmaanni (sexman in Swedish) for Harjakangas. Each village usually had one man who was a member of the Parish Council who saw that no one in his village was breaking th
2 CONC e law. When anyone in the village needed an official, Kustaa was likely the one whom people first contacted. He was himself, a man of good character and known in his community as being a fair and reliable man.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
