2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In 1901, Sandra lived at home in the village of Havingi on the Krekula farm.  Married Frank Evert Wahlroos on November 7, 1903 in Harjavalta, Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Came to USA onboard "Stockholm", departing Gothenburg on December 30, 1916 and entering NewYork on January 13, 1917.  Tekla A. and children Impi and Taisto travelled together.  Nearest relative in Finland listed as brother, Johann
2 CONC es Henriksson, Harjavalta, Finland and they were destined for Newport, New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1917, Sandra, Ginny and Ty came to America.  They came on the SS Stockholm on January 13, 1917 through Ellis Island, NY.  Sally and Kitty stayed with Frank's parents, Frank stayed with an aunt.  They came to the US in 1920.  Ai
2 CONC leen stayed with Sandra's parents from the age of 18 months until she was 16 when she moved to Newport.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mummu worked for Peerless Mfg Co. which made women's underware.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frank and Sandra became US citizens on February 11, 1960.  Both were almost 80 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sandra and daughter, Aileen, returned to Finland for a 5 week visit with relatives in 1971 when she was 90 years old.  At the time of her death, she was the oldest Finnish woman in Newport, NH.  She had been a member of the Americ
2 CONC an Finnish Club of Newport.
