2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT . Eeva Kristiina was last at Holy Communion on June 8, 1852. She died the following year of tuberculosis.  Kustaa Mattila and his family lived at Mattila farm in Harjakangas  (Ridgewoods) village, located in Noormarkku Luthern Par
2 CONC ish, Pori, Finland. He was born in Eura Parish and had moved from there to Noormarkkua   couple years before he married his first wife, Eeva Kristiina Mikkola. Kustaa became that farm owner at Mattila farm. In the late 1830’s Kust
2 CONC aa became the seksmaanni (sexman in Swedish) for Harjakangas.  Each village usually had one man who was a member of the Parish Council who saw that no one in his village was breaking the law. When anyone in the village needed an o
2 CONC fficial, Kustaa was likely the one whom people first contacted.  He was himself, a man of good character and known in his community as being a fair and reliable man. About 1840 Kustaa Mattila was elected as Parish Warden, being a 
2 CONC higher official of the parish. He retained his position of seksmanni as well. He held both positions until the late 1850’s.  Although Mattila was not a large farm, it was prosperous enough to support at least two farmhands and two
2 CONC  servant girls at a time. Contracts were usually negotiated in the autumn for the following   Year.  The hired people at Mattila usually there for two or three years before moving away. Kustaa and his two wives were usually in chu
2 CONC rch for Holy Communion only once each year, They were each recorded in the annual kinkeri (parish examination) as having a good understanding of their faith.   However, it was noted that Kustaa was surprising weak at reading and w
2 CONC riting. When it came to verbally explaining his faith, he did much better. The end of 1860, Kustaa and his second wife, Marja Sofia, were living at the Mattila farm.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
